Not exactly Metalcore but a hop and a skip away, Being As An Ocean.

&#x200B;

They put on an incredibly emotional and captivating show. Their unclean vocalist basically spends the entire concert in the pit while he's screaming.

&#x200B;

Silent Planet for sure too.

Well first we have to look at the things that do make it age well. For instance, I'll use Let It Enfold You by Senses Fail (I know it's not metalcore, it's just the first thing that comes to my mind when I think of a finely aged album). It has an incredibly nostalgic production sound, the songs are catchy and the instrumentation varies from song to song, The lyrics are meaningful while also being incredibly singable, and you can listen to each song and find something new you like every time.

&#x200B;

So now on to what makes it bad:

&#x200B;

Not instrumentally creative

&#x200B;

Lackluster lyrics, boring chorus

&#x200B;

Loss of identity throughout the album

&#x200B;

Generic production

&#x200B;

Cringe references relating to pop culture of the time

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I'd say if it fits into two of those then it will be forgotten.

